1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,603
Pro adds an invoicing workspace to the WooCommerce order screen.

2
00:00:04,603 --> 00:00:10,037
Billing and shipping details are stacked, with lightly shaded fields for inline editing.

3
00:00:10,037 --> 00:00:14,210
Keep a separate delivery address, or use the same address as billing.

4
00:00:15,510 --> 00:00:19,597
Add order references such as a purchase order or event date.

5
00:00:19,597 --> 00:00:22,319
Custom fields appear on your documents.

6
00:00:22,319 --> 00:00:28,600
Use Send to payment provider only for fields you want forwarded through a supported payment gateway.

7
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:33,521
Add headings and Markdown content to your document sections.

8
00:00:33,521 --> 00:00:35,996
Use the handles to change their order.

9
00:00:35,996 --> 00:00:42,570
The paper preview reflects section edits before you save the order, so you can check the wording and arrangement.

10
00:00:44,096 --> 00:00:47,839
Set a shared logo and company details under Invoicing.

11
00:00:47,839 --> 00:00:52,405
Choose paper size, compact item spacing, and a footer style.

12
00:00:52,405 --> 00:00:57,496
Assign a different saved layout to each document type when you need different designs.

13
00:00:58,833 --> 00:01:03,546
Use the WordPress block editor to design reusable PDF layouts.

14
00:01:03,546 --> 00:01:09,670
Arrange dynamic document areas with supported headings, paragraphs, images, and patterns.

15
00:01:09,670 --> 00:01:15,683
The item table has its own compact spacing control. Save the layout for future documents.

16
00:01:17,043 --> 00:01:22,544
Preview invoices, quotations, packing slips, and delivery orders from the order screen.

17
00:01:22,544 --> 00:01:27,310
Packing slips and delivery orders keep quantities without monetary values.

18
00:01:27,310 --> 00:01:31,723
Your assigned document number is separate from the WooCommerce order reference.

19
00:01:34,223 --> 00:01:38,407
Use the paired Preview and Download controls for each document.

20
00:01:38,407 --> 00:01:44,400
Credit notes describe existing WooCommerce refunds; they do not create a refund.

21
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:51,623
Payments continue through your installed WooCommerce gateway. Exporting a PDF does not charge the customer.
